From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: SurfaceImageSource

SurfaceImageSource did not exist: OneDrive's sign-in page draws its pictures with RNSVG into one and ended with an unhandled exception. A program now draws into it with its own device, through ISurfaceImageSourceNativeWithD2D (a Direct2D device context, or a DXGI surface of the Direct2D device) or ISurfaceImageSourceNative (a Direct3D device's surface). What it drew is read back at EndDraw into the pixels an Image shows.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/classes.idl b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/classes.idl
index db4659c..286067c 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/classes.idl
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/classes.idl
@@ -1213,6 +1213,14 @@ namespace Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls {
 }
 
 namespace Windows.UI.Xaml.Media.Imaging {
+    [contract(Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract, 1.0), uuid(62f7d416-c714-4c4c-8273-f839bc58135c)]
+    interface ISurfaceImageSource : IInspectable {}
+    [contract(Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract, 1.0), uuid(3ab2212a-ef65-4a5f-bfac-73993e8c12c9)]
+    interface ISurfaceImageSourceFactory : IInspectable {}
+    /* composable on Windows; marked activatable so that widl registers it */
+    [activatable(Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract, 1.0), contract(Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract, 1.0),
+     marshaling_behavior(agile), threading(both)]
+    runtimeclass SurfaceImageSource { [default] interface Windows.UI.Xaml.Media.Imaging.ISurfaceImageSource; }
     [contract(Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract, 1.0), uuid(d2dd9ed0-d3c5-4056-91b5-b7c1d1e8130e)]
     interface ISoftwareBitmapSource : IInspectable {}
     [contract(Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract, 1.0), uuid(31af3271-e3b4-442d-a341-4c0226b2725b)]
